<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">National Revolutionary Party</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1929–1938</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The National Revolutionary Party was the Mexican ruling party founded in 1929 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/plutarco-elias-calles">Plutarco Elías Calles</a> after the assassination of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alvaro-obregon">Álvaro Obregón</a>. It united revolutionary generals and regional political machines in one organisation so that the presidential succession could be settled peacefully. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lazaro-cardenas">Lázaro Cárdenas</a> reorganised it in 1938 as the Party of the Mexican Revolution, which became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/institutional-revolutionary-party">Institutional Revolutionary Party</a> in 1946.</p></div>
